 "summary": "All links up. Mission Control (Endpoint B) sends 22 commands 1.5 s apart, signed with the demo TEST KEYS (Ed25519 suite 0xFF02 unless noted, HMAC-SHA-256 suite 0xFF01 where noted): valid commands, commands altered after signing (command byte, priority, TTL, Timestamp, security_sequence, Authority Context, CRC), byte-identical replays, commands signed with keys the rover does not hold, an unknown key_id, an expired command, unauthorized and authorized roles, a wrong policy epoch, an unsigned command, a command without Authority Context, and a protected command carrying an unknown frame type. The rover (Endpoint A) verifies each one per PBS-SEC-B-01 and PBS-AUTH-01 and logs its disposition; tampering is applied by Endpoint B before the envelope is handed to ION and stands for modification in transit.",
